    "background_story": "Edward had always been fascinated by the written word. As a child, he spent hours scribbling stories and poetry in his notebooks. As he grew older, his passion for writing only intensified. He devoured books of all genres, analyzing the styles and techniques of his favorite authors. After completing his degree in creative writing, Edward moved to a small cabin in the woods to focus on his craft. For years, he wrote tirelessly, pouring his heart and soul into his work. His breakthrough novel, 'The Whispering Woods', became a bestseller, praised for its vivid descriptions and poignant characters. Edward's writing was not just a form of self-expression, but a way to connect with others and share his unique perspective on the world.",
